From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:11:20 -0700
Subject: [M156] GL: Force finish on IMG when copying within a texture

Original change's description:
> GL: Force finish on IMG when copying within a texture
>
> Forces a finish before performing a copy between different regions
> of the same texture to work around a driver bug on IMG hardware.
> Unfortunately a flush (or even forcefullyFlush) is not sufficient
> to avoid the driver issue.
>
> Fixed: chromium:552672183
> Change-Id: Id3f95f6d68291c43d528ec6913f9d0f40f16a593
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8620883
> Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>

(cherry picked from commit d9294ad1c0514a0cb889fa32eb5c39db3c1c38f0)

Bug: chromium:576948931,chromium:552672183
Change-Id: Id3f95f6d68291c43d528ec6913f9d0f40f16a593
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8685721
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): the M156 merge is used because the main
CL also conflicts here. Only adjacency conflicts were resolved: the new
finishBeforeSameTextureCopy entries are appended after this branch's
doubleClearForRobustInit/deferGlDeleteBuffers in FeaturesGL_autogen.h and
gl_features.json, and the ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION is inserted after
limitMaxBufferSizeTo1gb in InitializeFeatures. No logic changes.

